Judgment (Q1):  
A earns most weight because collective continuity is the overriding good;  
C receives substantial weight because sincerity matters once the duty is accepted;  
B carries little weight—it mistakes private emotion for the core issue.

Reasoning (Q2):  
A dominates because the society grounds morality in enacted cycles, independent of feeling;  
C has secondary weight: the form is fixed, but one can fulfill it without deceit;  
B has minimal weight—it undervalues what ritual teaches by doing.

